{"AccessTokenContext constructor checks Objects.requireNonNull(grantType, \"Null rawTokenId not allowed\") instead of validating rawTokenId, allowing null raw token IDs while checking grantType twice": 0.9691919088363647, "isAccessTokenId() returns false when embedded grant shortcut matches expectedGrantShortcut, rejecting valid encoded IDs while wrong shortcuts can pass": 0.9915120005607605, "initToken() resolves TokenContextEncoderProvider unconditionally and will cause NullPointerException in deployments that do not register the new SPI implementation, breaking legacy UUID token creation": 0.7291343808174133, "Token context encoder only derives SessionType from TRANSIENT vs online/offline, omitting ONLINE_TRANSIENT_CLIENT and OFFLINE_TRANSIENT_CLIENT cases needed for token-exchange flows where user session is persistent but client session is transient": 0.39964917302131653, "getTokenContextFromTokenId() hard-rejects any encoded context whose prefix is not exactly 6 characters long, failing on tokens with longer or richer prefixes and breaking backward compatibility": 0.3640124499797821, "Token exchange uses TokenContextEncoderProvider without fallback when provider is unavailable, causing failures in installations that don't register this SPI": 0.1689741462469101, "resolveLightweightAccessTokenRoles() dereferences session.getProvider(TokenContextEncoderProvider.class) without null check, causing NPE during token role resolution in deployments without the new SPI": 0.07352838665246964, "findValidSessionForAccessToken() always fetches TokenContextEncoderProvider before session lookup, breaking backward compatibility when SPI is absent and making legacy tokens unusable": 0.061550039798021317, "DefaultTokenContextEncoderProvider constructor stores provider/factory without null validation, enabling NPEs during token encoding/decoding": 0.20848406851291656, "encodeTokenId() assumes factory.getShortcutByGrantType() succeeds without guarding against uninitialized factory